# Pool extras — packages that ship in the apt pool on the installer
# ISO but are NEVER installed in any chroot (live, installer ramdisk,
# or target debootstrap).  Available to apt at install time and
# post-install via the cdrom: source.
#
# Contract:
#   1. Each entry is resolved by `dependencytree.resolve_packages` in
#      Pass VII (see scripts/build.py) the same way pkg.list /
#      live.list / installer.list deb-arm entries are.  All transitive
#      Depends are pulled in and end up in `selected_pkgs` → built by
#      the source-build pipeline → land in `repo/` → ship in
#      `staging/pool/`.
#   2. Pass VII calls resolve_packages with `check_conflicts=False`
#      and `validate_selection` skips Breaks/Conflicts where either
#      side is in `pool_extras_pkg_names`.  This lets mutually-
#      conflicting packages (e.g. `grub-pc` + `grub-efi-amd64`)
#      coexist in the pool — apt on the target enforces conflicts at
#      install time, picking exactly one.
#   3. `cmd_build_iso_installer` subtracts pool extras from
#      `base_include` so debootstrap does NOT install them on the
#      target.  They stay in `_pool_whitelist` so the .debs ship in
#      the cdrom pool.
#
# What this is for:
#   - Mutually-exclusive packages where install-time selection
#     happens on the target (not at build time).  Canonical example:
#     bootloader metas where grub-installer picks `grub-pc` (BIOS) or
#     `grub-efi-amd64` (EFI) based on firmware mode.
#   - Optional packages we want available on a fresh install without
#     network access — operator can `apt-get install <name>` from the
#     cdrom source post-install.
#
# History (2026-05-13 / -14):
#   - Phase D (commit 875200e) swapped `grub-pc` (META) for
#     `grub-pc-bin` + `grub-efi-amd64-bin` in `pkg.list` so an EFI
#     install would have both `-bin` packages available.  Side
#     effect: the META .debs (built by the grub2 source build, so
#     present in `repo/`) stopped getting copied into
#     `staging/pool/` because `_pool_whitelist = selected_pkgs -
#     live_excl` no longer included them.  Both BIOS
#     (`apt-install grub-pc`) and EFI (`apt-install grub-efi-amd64`)
#     `grub-installer` runs failed with "no installation candidate".
#   - First fix attempt (the file existed in an earlier shape) was a
#     manifest of names whose `.deb`s already happened to be in
#     `repo/` — bypassed the resolver entirely.  Worked for the grub
#     case but had no path to add packages whose source we hadn't
#     built yet (e.g. open-vm-tools).  Redesigned 2026-05-14 to go
#     through the resolver with conflicts disabled — same dep
#     resolution as everything else in the build, plus the conflict
#     bypass for genuinely-pool-only entries.

# ─── Bootloader metas ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# grub-installer apt-installs whichever fits the target's firmware
# mode at install time.  The Conflict between them is enforced by
# apt on the target — both .debs sit indexed in /cdrom/pool side by
# side here.
grub-pc
grub-efi-amd64

# ─── VMware guest tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `finish-install`'s `hw-detect` runs `apt-install open-vm-tools` on
# VMware hypervisors.  Available in the pool here so that probe
# succeeds on VMware targets (no-op on bare-metal / non-VMware
# hypervisors).  Source builds normally — small dependency closure
# (libdrm2, libmspack0, libtirpc3, libxmlsec1, ethtool, zerofree on
# top of what we already ship).
open-vm-tools
open-vm-tools-desktop

# ─── Console keymap configuration ──────────────────────────────────
# `base-installer`'s `apt-install` queues both `console-setup` and
# `keyboard-configuration` for /target so the installed system has a
# working console keymap matching the locale picked at install time.
# `keyboard-configuration` Depends `xkb-data (>= 2.35.1~) (<< 2.35.1A)`
# — `xkb-data` lives in source package `xkeyboard-config`, which
# Pass VII will pull into the source-build pipeline.  Without these
# in the pool, base-installer logs `Failed to install
# keyboard-configuration into /target/: 100` and `Failed to install
# console-setup into /target/: 100` (verified 2026-05-14 install
# run, both BIOS and EFI).  Not pre-installed in pkg.list because
# the live image doesn't need them — they're target-side only.
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
xkb-data
